	<package>
		<name>MacOS Microsoft Outlook</name>
		<application_name>Microsoft Outlook</application_name>
		<bundleId>com.microsoft.Outlook</bundleId>
		<currentVersionReleaseDate>September 16, 2026</currentVersionReleaseDate>
		<icon_image>https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Purple211/v4/f5/11/eb/f511ebca-b848-e913-f26b-a6519656e8b8/Outlook_macOS-0-0-85-220-0-0-0-6-0-2x.png/512x512bb.png</icon_image>
		<minimumOsVersion>14.0</minimumOsVersion>
		<releaseNotes>Resolved Issues: 
•  Mail: The unread-count badge in the Dock now initializes correctly at startup.  
•  Mail: Improved the experience for viewing and interacting with Loop components in Outlook messages.
•  Add-ins: Attachments added or removed by add-ins now synchronize more reliably, including during rapid or overlapping draft saves. 
 
Feature Updates: 
•  Calendar: Outlook Settings now let users manage work hours and work-location schedules for supported accounts.
•  Calendar: Users can choose whether accepted invitations are removed from the Inbox and whether conflicting events are automatically declined on supported accounts.
•  Mail: Replies forwards, initial content, and signatures now automatically follow the left-to-right or right-to-left direction of the referenced message.
•  Mail: Added Editor Settings to customize spelling and grammar by language. 
•  Mail: Added a remove button to make deleting recipients easier when composing emails. 
•  Mail: Paste Options now supports converting Markdown to rich text. 
•  Mail: Paragraph Options now provide better control over advanced formatting.
•  Contacts: Administrators can use cloud policy to control whether presence indicators appear for recipients and contacts in Outlook.
•  Copilot: Eligible users can now see linked Microsoft account subscriptions associated with their Copilot account in Outlook Settings. 
•  Security: Outlook can automatically inherit an appropriate sensitivity label from labeled attachments 
•  General: Users can right-click Mail, Calendar, and People icons in the left rail to open them in a separate window. 
•  General: Users can personalize Outlook by choosing an accent color.</releaseNotes>
		<version>16.113</version>
		<app_store_url>https://apps.apple.com/us/app/microsoft-outlook/id985367838?mt=12&amp;uo=4</app_store_url>
	</package>
